#: ../../../reference/interfaces/ros-opt-data-interface.md:2
msgid "ros-opt-data interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/ros-opt-data-interface.md:4
msgid ""
"The `ros-opt-data` interface creates a read-only mount from within a snap to "
"the standard Robot Operating System (ROS) directory (`/opt/ros/*`) on the "
"host system, enabling robotics-based snaps to share ROS robot data, such as "
"the URDF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/ros-opt-data-interface.md:6
msgid ""
"This interface cannot currently be used on Ubuntu Core. Requires snapd "
"version *2.62+*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/ros-opt-data-interface.md:8
msgid ""
"To add this interface to a snap, define a plug in the app section of its "
"[snapcraft.yaml](https://documentation.ubuntu.com/snapcraft/stable/reference/"
"project-file/anatomy-of-snapcraft-yaml/) for the application that requires "
"ROS data access:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/ros-opt-data-interface.md:10
msgid ""
"apps:\n"
"  hello-world:\n"
"    command: ./hello.sh\n"
"    plugs: [ros-opt-data]   #this is the new interface plug name\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/ros-opt-data-interface.md:17
msgid "Mount location"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/ros-opt-data-interface.md:19
msgid ""
"This interface uses the standard snap location for mounted directories: `/"
"var/lib/snapd/hostfs/`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/ros-opt-data-interface.md:22
msgid ""
"For example, if this interface is used to access `/opt/ros/noetic/robot-urdf/"
"models` on the host machine, it will be found within the snap at `/var/lib/"
"snapd/hostfs/opt/ros/noetic/robot-urdf/models`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/ros-opt-data-interface.md:24
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/ros-opt-data-interface.md:26
msgid ""
"**{ref}`Auto-connect <explanation-interfaces-interface-auto-connection>`**: "
"yes</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/ros-opt-data-interface.md:26
msgid "</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/ros-opt-data-interface.md:28
msgid "Code examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/ros-opt-data-interface.md:30
msgid ""
"The following is a simple _hello-world_ example that includes an additional "
"plug/slot mechanism for enabling the `ros-opt-data` interface. We're going "
"to modify this example to show how the interface can access ROS-related data "
"on the host system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/ros-opt-data-interface.md:32
msgid "The initial snapcraft.yaml is as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/ros-opt-data-interface.md:34
msgid ""
"name: hello-world\n"
"version: '0.1'\n"
"summary: A simple hello world application\n"
"description: |\n"
"  A simple hello world application.\n"
"base: core22\n"
"\n"
"grade: devel\n"
"confinement: strict\n"
"\n"
"apps:\n"
"  hello-world:\n"
"    command: ./hello.sh\n"
"\n"
"parts:\n"
"  hello-world:\n"
"    plugin: dump\n"
"    source: files\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/ros-opt-data-interface.md:55
msgid ""
"When the snap is built, installed and executed, it runs the following "
"`hello.sh` script (which for now only outputs  “hello world”)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/ros-opt-data-interface.md:57
msgid ""
"#!/bin/bash\n"
"echo \"hello world\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/ros-opt-data-interface.md:62
msgid ""
"We now want to change the above script to output the contents of a "
"`setup.bash` file located in the host's `/opt/ros` directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/ros-opt-data-interface.md:64
msgid ""
"The following modification assumes we're using ROS Noetic Ninjemys, but the "
"file location can be adapted for any other ROS distro:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/ros-opt-data-interface.md:66
msgid ""
"#!/bin/bash\n"
"cat /var/lib/snapd/hostfs/opt/ros/noetic/setup.bash\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/ros-opt-data-interface.md:71
msgid "We now modify the snapcraft.yaml to insert the new plug:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/ros-opt-data-interface.md:73
msgid ""
"name: hello-world\n"
"version: '0.1'\n"
"summary: A simple hello world application\n"
"description: |\n"
"  A simple hello world application.\n"
"base: core22\n"
"\n"
"grade: devel # must be 'stable' to release into candidate/stable channels\n"
"confinement: strict\n"
"\n"
"apps:\n"
"  hello-world:\n"
"    command: ./hello.sh\n"
"    plugs: [ros-opt-data]\n"
"\n"
"parts:\n"
"  hello-world:\n"
"    plugin: dump\n"
"    source: files\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/ros-opt-data-interface.md:95
msgid ""
"When the new snap is built, installed and executed, the output will now be "
"the contents of `/opt/ros/noetic/setup.bash`."
msgstr ""

